WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.980
Today we are going to use NVIDIA’s&nbsp;
new AI to create absolutely magical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.220
time lapse videos that were otherwise&nbsp;
nearly impossible to make. Until now.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:24.900
Watching a video of a landscape in real time&nbsp;
is a smooth experience, but not as interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:31.500
as seemingly, nothing is happening. Now,&nbsp;
speeding them up creates us a time lapse video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:40.320
this is finally interesting, however, then this&nbsp;
happens. Oh yes, we get too much flickering.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:48.000
This is not for human consumption, that’s for&nbsp;
sure. If only an AI-based algorithm existed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.720
could somehow take the essence of the changes&nbsp;
in this video, but make it smooth as well.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:02.940
Now, of course that sounds flat out impossible.&nbsp;
Why? Well, in these time lapse videos, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:10.380
experience drastic weather changes within a day,&nbsp;
photos for some days are missing, and even worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:16.680
occlusions might happen. Now, let’s have a&nbsp;
look at a previous method trying to do that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:24.240
Hmm. Something is happening here, it is&nbsp;
able to keep the weather conditions stable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:33.000
so we get no more flickering. However, do you&nbsp;
see it? Growing is clearly happening, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:39.780
details have been washed out so much that the&nbsp;
most interesting part of the video is now gone.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.960
I am not that hopeful that this is&nbsp;
possible to solve well, but just in case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:53.280
let’s have a look at NVIDIA’s new AI and see&nbsp;
what it is made of. This is the input, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:02:01.260
wow! The new method does an absolutely outstanding&nbsp;
job at keeping the weather conditions stable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:07.320
but in the meantime, also showing us&nbsp;
sharp footage of this amazing growth.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.460
Now let’s compare it to the previous method. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:17.820
my goodness, there is no contest&nbsp;
here. So much better. Loving it!

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:24.060
Let’s have a look at another example of this&nbsp;
valley and then, I will show you that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.660
technique also has some more superpowers.&nbsp;
As expected, the input video has way too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.360
much going on, so now, let’s ask the new&nbsp;
method to boil it down to its essence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:43.860
That is absolutely incredible. Look,&nbsp;
smooth and detailed at the same time.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:49.320
And yes, I promised some&nbsp;
superpowers, so what are those?

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:56.580
This technique can not only stabilize the weather&nbsp;
conditions and create smooth and detailed videos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:04.260
but, one, depending on our artistic goals, it even&nbsp;
gives us the tools to control the time of day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:10.260
And if we wish to think bigger, we&nbsp;
can also control the time of year.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:21.120
But all that is nothing compared to my favorite,&nbsp;
so hold on to your papers for trends. If there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.880
are structural changes in a landscape&nbsp;
or a city, for instance, at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.640
this building has been repainted, and&nbsp;
now we can decide to forget about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.980
and keep it as if it never even&nbsp;
happened, or we can even decide to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:45.420
use its new appearance for the entirety of&nbsp;
the year. Even before it was painted. Wow!

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:51.900
And we can also account for growth. This&nbsp;
growth can take place as the video progresses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:58.800
or it can be fixed in time.&nbsp;
This is so good, I love it.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:04.620
And now, time for some interesting&nbsp;
tidbits. This technique is based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:10.200
the legendary StyleGAN system, which is&nbsp;
able to synthesize these photorealistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.220
humans and other things in a&nbsp;
somewhat controllable manner.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:21.960
Also, I bet the authors had a few conversations&nbsp;
asking each other “how on Earth do we put all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:28.380
this video information into one stationary&nbsp;
image in the paper”, this concept is a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:34.860
harder to convey there, so I am so happy to&nbsp;
be able to show you these videos instead.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:44.160
And what I also loved is this. Look. Are you&nbsp;
seeing what I am seeing? My goodness. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:50.640
of these datasets have not only a few days&nbsp;
missing here and there, there are often a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:58.080
